thub.com/repos/neovim/neovim/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/deployments","created_at":"2014-01-31T13:39:22Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T09:22:08Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-13T05:17:45Z","git_url":"git://github.com/neovim/neovim.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:neovim/neovim.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim","homepage":"https://neovim.io","size":355316,"stargazers_count":94890,"watchers_count":94890,"language":"Vim Script","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":6465,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2020,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["api","c","lua","neovim","nvim","text-editor","vim"],"visibility":"public","forks":6465,"open_issues":2020,"watchers":94890,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"- `nvim --version`:\r\n  - first seen on `NVIM v0.4.4; Build type: Release`\r\n  - reproduced on fresh master: `NVIM v0.5.0-dev+1075-g02a3c4179`\r\n- `vim -u DEFAULTS` (version: ) behaves differently?\r\n  - yes, it shows `E282: Cannot read from \"DEFAULTS\"` but also it doesn't reproduce the crash. Did you mean `-U DEFAULTS` perhaps?\r\n- Operating system/version:\r\n  - `Manjaro Linux x86_64`\r\n  - kernel: `5.4.89-1-MANJARO`\r\n- Terminal name/version: `alacritty 0.7.1 (a852eb85)`\r\n- `$TERM`: `xterm-256color`\r\n\r\nSeems related to https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/13072.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\r\n1. `:e ~/.vimrc` (I haven't had success reproducing with empty buffer)\r\n2. `<C-w>v` (make a vertical split)\r\n3. `<C-w>l` (move to the right window)\r\n  - (alternatively you can `:set splitright` before making the vertical split but I guess the listed way is more minimal)\r\n4. `<C-w>|` (maximize horizontally)\r\n5. resize the terminal window in any way\r\n\r\n### Actual behaviour\r\n`nvim` crashes with:\r\n```\r\ncorrupted size vs. prev_size\r\nAborted (core dumped)\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote: Right after the maximizing, you can see the first line overflowing into the buffer border (ie. `seset` should be `s|set`). This seems to be a good indicator of whether it will crash later or not.\r\n![bleed](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/149425/107219289-27d21600-6a11-11eb-9388-50a3a0f1b3a1.png)\r\n\r\nNote 2: It also shows this error message when trying to exit Vim normally instead of resizing the terminal window.\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour\r\nNot crashing; also perhaps not bleeding the text into the buffer border.\r\n\r\n### GDB backtrace (from the `master` version, not `0.4.4`):\r\n```\r\nThread 2 \"nvim\" received signal SIGABRT, Aborted.\r\n[Switching to Thread 0x7fefcebdd640 (LWP 612961)]\r\n0x00007fefcf0da615 in raise () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n\r\n(gdb) bt\r\n#0  0x00007fefcf0da615 in raise () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n#1  0x00007fefcf0c3862 in abort () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n#2  0x00007fefcf11c5e8 in __libc_message () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n#3  0x00007fefcf12427a in malloc_printerr () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n#4  0x00007fefcf125176 in unlink_chunk.constprop () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n#5  0x00007fefcf1259cb in _int_free () from /usr/lib/libc.so.6\r\n#6  0x0000557130817821 in xfree (ptr=<optimized out>) at ../src/nvim/memory.c:119\r\n#7  0x00005571308ec135 in destroy_cells (grid=grid@entry=0x7fefc80117c0) at ../src/nvim/ugrid.c:98\r\n#8  0x00005571308ee399 in ugrid_resize (grid=0x7fefc80117c0, width=131, height=56) at ../src/nvim/ugrid.c:30\r\